{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MarkovTraceRatioExact","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MarkovTraceRatioExact","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.gram_entry_proportional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.gram_entry_proportional","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-ratio-exact.lean#L67-L77","doc":"Corollary: Gram matrix entries computed from Markov traces are\nproportional to Gram matrix entries from Jones polynomials.\nThe proportionality constant is `C²` (one factor per braid in\nthe inner product `tr_M(β_i · β_j)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.markov_trace_ratio_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.markov_trace_ratio_exact","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-ratio-exact.lean#L42-L65","doc":"For a fixed strand count `n` and substrate `q`, the ratio of\nMarkov traces of two braids equals the ratio of their Jones\npolynomials. The normalisation factor `C(n, q)` cancels. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:markov-trace-ratio-exact","label":"prop:markov-trace-ratio-exact","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-ratio-exact.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.jonesNormFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.jonesNormFactor","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-ratio-exact.lean#L33-L40","doc":"The normalisation factor `C(n, q)` relating the mass-formula\nMarkov trace to the Jones polynomial. Its exact form is\n`(-q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2})^{n-1} · (-q^{-3/2})^{-w(β)}`, but\nthe key property is that it depends on `n` (strand count) and\n`q` (substrate), NOT on the braid word `β`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}